{
  "_readme": "Manual corrections applied on top of prep/analyze.py. All coordinates are normalised (0..1) image coords. Cells are addressed as r<row>c<col> (see debug/grid.png). Per cell: add_boundaries / remove_boundaries = x positions of spine borders to split / merge; standing / flat / exclude = [x0,y0,x1,y1] rects forcing a region type. objects.add = extra objects, objects.drop_auto = ids of auto-detected objects to discard. grid.posts_x / grid.shelves_y replace the detected frame lines (rarely needed). flat_books = exact [x0,y0,x1,y1] of single lying books (replace overlapping auto ones). boundaries = full manual list of spine borders for a cell; tops = [[x0,x1,y]] sets the top of spines whose centre is in x0..x1.",
